N5008 [class.cdtor]/4: a virtual call from a constructor or destructor
dispatches to the overrider of the class whose constructor/destructor runs.
Destructors used to install their virtual pointers AFTER the body, so ~B saw
D::f; a class with virtual bases installs nothing in its base-object
destructor, and its bases' pointers now hold the complete object's
construction vtables (Itanium C++ ABI 2.6.2) while it is constructed or
destroyed.
